{
  "$comment": [
    "Approval at the unit of work, not the keystroke. Read .claude/hooks/approved_scope.py.",
    "",
    "Per-file prompts are the right shape for an unplanned edit to a guard and the wrong",
    "shape for an approved programme of work — six agents once produced roughly 1,500",
    "prompts for work the owner had already approved, and approving a thousand prompts is",
    "not approving anything. A scope moves the approval to the same unit as the plan.",
    "",
    "Ships EMPTY. Every core path prompts until the owner writes a scope and approves this",
    "file, which is the one prompt that matters.",
    "",
    "A scope is usable only if it has all five fields, gives a real reason, and expires",
    "within 45 days. Malformed, uncited, unbounded or expired waives nothing and the prompts",
    "return. A broad pattern never reaches a system-altering area — migrations, auth, the",
    "audit ledger, deploy, the workflows, the rulesets and the scanner config are covered",
    "only by a pattern that NAMES them, so 'backend/**' pre-approves module work and stops",
    "at the migrations folder. Pre-approving something dangerous is allowed and has to be",
    "said out loud.",
    "",
    "No scope can ever waive .claude/ — widening the agent's own authority is guarded by a",
    "mechanism that does not depend on the agent's code being correct.",
    "",
    "A scope buys silence at the KEYSTROKE, never at the gate: the meta-guard still demands",
    "the owner's label on the pull request, and CI is untouched.",
    "",
    "Example:",
    "  {",
    "    \"name\": \"billing module, slices 1-3\",",
    "    \"cites\": \"docs/decisions/0013-billing-boundary.md\",",
    "    \"reason\": \"Approved on 2026-09-21: build the billing module and its guards.\",",
    "    \"paths\": [\"backend/**\", \"tests/guards/**\", \"docs/decisions/**\"],",
    "    \"expires\": \"2026-10-15\"",
    "  }"
  ],
  "scopes": []
}
